          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "D9 makes `anchor id` part of the obligation id, but D2 explicitly says obligations are derived per entry and are not multiplied by cite count. Downstream derivation cannot know whether to emit one obligation per declaration item, reusing its test group across all cited anchors, or one obligation per `(entry, anchor, kind, item)`. That changes obligation counts, binding shape, and totality semantics, so the ADR needs one consistent identity model before spec/types can translate it.",
              "severity": "P1",
